---
// /en/ (переработка 2026-07-12): не перевод главной, а адаптация под expat/corporate-
// аудиторию. Отличия от RU (осознанные): интро-звонок 30 минут, контакты без телефона,
// расписание в CET, цены только в евро, ссылки на EN-страницы. Структура и голос
// сверены с актуальными RU-страницами (/ и /home/).
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---

<Page
  title="Valeriy Karasaev · Psychologist and Executive Coach · Therapy in English"
  description="Gestalt therapist and executive coach for professionals and expats. Burnout, relocation, identity, career transitions, leadership loneliness. Online sessions in English, 60 €. Free 30-minute intro call."
  lang="en"
  translation="/"
  hideCta={true}
>
  <div class="page-head" style="text-align: center;">
    <!-- «Правки-6» п.15: тот же естественный портрет, что на RU-главной.
         Прежняя аватарка сохранена: public/images/photo/avatar.jpg -->
    <img src="/images/photo/home-hero.jpg" alt="Valeriy Karasaev" width="108" height="108" style="border-radius: 50%; border: 2px solid var(--gold); margin-bottom: 18px; object-fit: cover; object-position: center 15%;" />
    <div class="kicker">Psychologist · Gestalt Therapist · Executive Coach</div>
    <h1 class="page-title">Therapy in English, for people who carry a lot</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      I help adults get through a crisis or a major transition - and find new ground.
      I don't promise fast. I promise honest. In practice since 2014; before that -
      17 years in international business, including 5 years living and working in Germany.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-group">
      <a href={site.en.telegramFreeCall} class="btn btn-primary">Free 30-min intro call</a>
      <a href={'mailto:' + site.email} class="btn btn-outline">Email me</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="meta-line"><span class="meta-num">01</span><span class="meta-label">What brings people to me</span></div>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Burnout that doesn't look like burnout - everything is fine on paper, and empty inside.
      Relocation that was supposed to be an adventure and turned into losing your footing.
      A career that stopped making sense. Leadership loneliness: being the one everyone relies on,
      with no one to talk to. Relationships stretched across cultures and time zones.
    </p>
    <p>
      I know this territory from both sides. I spent 17 years in international corporations -
      Abbott, BMW, Bosch - leading teams of up to 300 people across 30 countries, based in Moscow
      and then Frankfurt. I have been through relocation, divorce, burnout and an identity crisis
      myself - and worked through them in my own therapy, 12 years and over 1,000 hours of it.
      I don't need your world explained to me. I have lived in it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="meta-line"><span class="meta-num">02</span><span class="meta-label">What I work with</span></div>
  <div class="wk" style="max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto 8px;">
    <details>
      <summary><span class="wk-t">Burnout and chronic stress</span></summary>
      <div class="wk-body">You took the vacation. It didn't help. Everything still runs on the outside; inside it went quiet long ago. This is not laziness - the shape of your life got too small, like an old coat. We look for where exactly it pinches.</div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="wk-t">Loss of meaning, existential emptiness</span></summary>
      <div class="wk-body">Goals achieved, zero joy. At 3 a.m. the question "what is all this for" arrives - and silence answers. I don't hand out new meaning. I help you hear what you actually want.</div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="wk-t">Expat life: identity, adaptation, loneliness</span></summary>
      <div class="wk-body">Home stayed there, and you are here. The language is foreign, your status got reset, your friends live in a messenger. "Who am I now" is not a rhetorical question. I have lived through emigration myself and work with it constantly.</div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="wk-t">Divorce, separation, recovery after a breakup</span></summary>
      <div class="wk-body">Anger, guilt, relief, grief - all at once, and all of it feeling somehow "wrong". I know what it is to reassemble yourself. Not the old you. A different one.</div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="wk-t">Career transitions: out of corporate, into your own thing</span></summary>
      <div class="wk-body">Leaving is scary, staying is unbearable. The head keeps calculating risks; the body decided long ago. We look at what holds you: money, fear - or grief for the life you will have to let go of.</div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="wk-t">Leadership loneliness, the weight of responsibility</span></summary>
      <div class="wk-body">You can't complain to your team - you are their anchor. Upwards is where they evaluate you. One hour a week where you don't have to be strong. I spent 17 years in that role.</div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="wk-t">Relationship patterns that keep repeating</span></summary>
      <div class="wk-body">Partners change, the script stays the same. Closeness - escape. Resentment - silence. We look not at "him" or "her", but at how you build contact.</div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="wk-t">Men's experience: vulnerability, aggression, self-worth</span></summary>
      <div class="wk-body">Anger with nowhere to go. Weakness that must not show. Here you can be angry, cry and stay silent. For real. Without shame.</div>
    </details>
  </div>

  <div class="meta-line"><span class="meta-num">03</span><span class="meta-label">How I work</span></div>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      My core method is Gestalt therapy - working with what happens in contact, here and now.
      A psychoanalytic lens (MSc in Psychology, HSE University) helps to see recurring life patterns.
      Coaching tools (Erickson International, ICF-accredited) come in when structure and concrete
      steps are needed. 2,500+ hours of professional training altogether. I ask direct,
      sometimes uncomfortable questions - and I can hold what comes up: shame, anger, fear, emptiness.
      More about the process: <a href="/en/therapy/">how therapy works</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="meta-line"><span class="meta-num">04</span><span class="meta-label">Format and fees</span></div>
  <div class="spec">
    <div class="spec-row"><span class="spec-key">Session</span><span class="spec-val">50 minutes · online</span></div>
    <div class="spec-row"><span class="spec-key">Fee</span><span class="spec-val">60 € per session</span></div>
    <div class="spec-row"><span class="spec-key">Schedule</span><span class="spec-val">{site.en.schedule}</span></div>
    <div class="spec-row"><span class="spec-key">Payment</span><span class="spec-val">PayPal · IBAN · card</span></div>
    <div class="spec-row"><span class="spec-key">Languages</span><span class="spec-val">English · Russian</span></div>
  </div>

  <div class="meta-line"><span class="meta-num">05</span><span class="meta-label">Group</span></div>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Together with my colleague Irina, I run an English-speaking therapy group -
      <a href="/en/groups/work-ambition/">«Work, People, Ambition»</a> - about work that is never
      just work: ambition, recognition, competition, burnout and what we actually want.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="meta-line"><span class="meta-num">06</span><span class="meta-label">Credentials, in short</span></div>
  <div class="spec">
    <div class="spec-row"><span class="spec-key">MSc in Psychology, psychoanalytic track</span><span class="spec-val">HSE University · 2015-2018</span></div>
    <div class="spec-row"><span class="spec-key">Gestalt therapist · 4-year program, 733 hours</span><span class="spec-val">Moscow Gestalt Institute · 2017-2021</span></div>
    <div class="spec-row"><span class="spec-key">Certified coach, ICF-accredited</span><span class="spec-val">Erickson International · 2014-2015</span></div>
    <div class="spec-row"><span class="spec-key">Own therapy</span><span class="spec-val">12 years · 1,000+ hours</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>Diplomas, certificates and the full list: <a href="/en/credentials/">credentials with scans</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="meta-line"><span class="meta-num">07</span><span class="meta-label">Reading</span></div>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      I write about burnout, transitions and staying alive at work - no advice, no tidy wisdom
      at the end. English essays are collected in <a href="/en/articles/">Articles</a>;
      most of my writing lives in Russian on
      <a href="https://t.me/valera_outloud" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Telegram</a> and
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/karasaev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="cta-final">
    <div class="cta-title">Free 30-minute intro call</div>
    <div class="cta-sub">Meet, ask anything, see if we click. No strings attached</div>
    <div class="btn-group" style="margin: 0;">
      <a href={site.en.telegramFreeCall} class="btn btn-primary">Message me on Telegram</a>
      <a href={'mailto:' + site.email} class="btn btn-outline">{site.email}</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Page>
